# Bytecode Python writes beside the helper when it runs. It is *generated*, never
# *installed*: it embeds the absolute path it was compiled from, so committing it would
# put machine-specific bytes into an install whose whole premise is that every byte is
# identical everywhere. This file ships with the engine so that premise holds in the
# adopter's repo too, whatever their own ignore rules happen to be.
__pycache__/
